Problem: Longest Repeating Character Replacement (LC 424)

Pattern: Variable Size Sliding Window + Hash Map

Approach:

Use a frequency map to count characters in the current window.
Keep track of the highest frequency (maxFreq) seen in the window.
Expand the window by moving right.
If:
(window size - maxFreq) > k
the window is invalid, so:
Decrease the frequency of s[left].
Move left forward.
Update the maximum window length.
Return the maximum length.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(1) (since there are only a limited number of possible characters, e.g., uppercase English letters)